cff-version: 1.2.0
title: UniBuc Computational Physics Coursework
message: If you use this material, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Paul-Adrian
    family-names: Gogîță
    affiliation: Faculty of Physics, University of Bucharest
repository-code: https://github.com/PaulGoG/UniBuc-Computational-Physics-Coursework
abstract: >-
  Computational physics coursework of a BSc (2017-2021) and MSc (2021-2023) at
  the Faculty of Physics, University of Bucharest, rewritten in Julia as
  self-checking scripts: numerical integration, chaotic dynamics, Monte Carlo,
  optics, cosmology, radiation-matter interaction, nuclear masses, fission
  observables, DOAS remote sensing and a radiological screening exercise. The
  material as originally submitted is kept on the legacy branch.
keywords:
  - computational physics
  - coursework
  - numerical methods
  - nuclear physics
  - cosmology
  - Julia
license: MIT
